abstract: A combined study of spectral bounds and their information limits in Pauli contextuality. It
  integrates a Lean 4 formalization of the previously known spectral floor, configurations attaining exact
  degrees 75, 480 and 729344 with finite Lean certificates, and explicit cospectral sign carriers whose
  completion spectra differ. A four-qubit C3 pair has completion cubic traces 14976 and 15360 and different
  binary completion minima; a graph family settles case C3 for every number of qubits from four on, with a
  Lean proof; variants settle all nine vertex cases, proving Jonah's Conjecture E (outside case C3 by a
  self-contained paper proof, checked by exact computation). The manuscript
  distinguishes kernel-checked statements, paper proofs, executable counts, prior work, and open questions.
keywords:
- quantum contextuality
- Pauli group
- symplectic polar space
- Kochen-Specker theorem
- Clifford hierarchy
- bent functions
- Lean 4
- formal verification
- spectral invariants
- cospectrality
- Pauli completion
